title: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Run the connection test and save
route: /emr
intro: Step 3 of 'Connect a system': three read-only checks run one after the other, then 'Connect {name}' saves the system. In the demo the test always passes. Reconnect runs the very same three checks.
dir: TD
also: Production failures below come from the PRD (09 integrations) and are not simulated by the demo.
---
overlay o1 "Connect a system, step 3 of 3: Test\nRead-only. Nothing is written back until a person approves it."

group gTest "Connection test"
  process k1 "Reaching the system\nAbout 0.8 seconds a check: spinner, then a green tick"
  process k2 "Signing in with read-only access"
  process k3 "Reading one test record"
  toast t1 "'The test passed. Access is read-only, and nothing is written back.'"
endgroup

ext x1 "The system answers\nDemo: simulated with a demo record"
decision q1 "Can the test fail?"
endx f1 "Production only: sign-in rejected, a sign-in challenge, or the system unreachable\nThe feed pauses and a person is asked to fix it"
click b0 "'Connect {name}' is dimmed until the last check passes"
click b1 "Click 'Connect {name}'\nFor example 'Connect Lab results · Site B'"

group gSave "What is saved"
  store s1 "New system on the list\nStatus Connected, last sync now, connected since today, the contact, write-back off (its row says 'Read only')"
  store s2 "Files pulled tile goes up by 5"
  agent a1 "Reader logs 'Tested the read-only connection to {name} and found 5 files to pull'"
  toast t2 "'{name} is connected'\n'Read-only. Nothing is written back.'"
endgroup

end e1 "Pop-up closes\nThe new row sits at the end of Connection health"
click cx "Click 'Cancel', click the X, press Escape, or click the dimmed area"
endx e2 "Test stops, nothing is saved\nThere is no 'Back' on this step"
goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › Sync now"
goto g2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Open the Manage drawer"
goto g3 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Reconnect a system"

o1 --> k1 --> k2 --> k3 --> t1
k1 -.-> x1
k3 -.-> g3
t1 --> q1
q1 -->|Demo: never| b0 --> b1
q1 -->|Production| f1
b1 --> s1 & s2 & a1 & t2
s1 --> e1
t2 --> e1
e1 --> g1 & g2
o1 -.-> cx --> e2
